  "contract": [
    "One cancellable source factory and one candidate pass. The raw projection is captured after source-coordinate mapping and before local L2; the kept projection comes from the same pass.",
    "Only display fields are retained; no source contexts, bodies or scoring records are stored in the comparison pool. The combined raw/kept pool has 100000-row and 32 MiB conservative-size bounds.",
    "Source/semantic errors, cancellation, projection bounds and invalid/failed/panicking scorer batches prevent a suppression summary.",
    "The in-process threshold is frozen; verification, index side effects and remote L2 sidecars are excluded from the comparison API.",
    "CLI default fingerprint grouping retains an identity if any context survives; --no-dedupe counts individual accepted candidate rows. Multiset occurrence keys prevent a surviving duplicate from hiding another suppressed occurrence."
  ],
  "ci": {
    "job": "native-acquisition",
    "new_commands": [
      "python3 scripts/check_compare_contract.py \"$RUNNER_TEMP/prowl-acquisition\"",
      "python3 scripts/check_semantic_contract.py \"$RUNNER_TEMP/prowl-acquisition\""
    ],
    "external_run": "not executed"
  },
  "limits": [
    "Results compare observed candidates, not an atomic filesystem snapshot, real model quality, credential validity or business lift.",
    "Native inference uses an owned loopback stub; L2 uses the embedded model. No real provider, production tenant or deployment was exercised.",
    "CLI comparison remains a text summary with the existing stdin/OCR restriction. Source/read and model errors return 2 without a percentage."
